title: 'snowbridge: Ethereum Gloas support in the beacon light client'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds Gloas (Glamsterdam) support to the Snowbridge Ethereum beacon light client.

    EIP-7688 turns `BeaconState` and `BeaconBlockBody` into progressive containers, so every
    generalized index moves: `finalized_checkpoint.root` 169 -> 735, `current_sync_committee`
    86 -> 2945, `next_sync_committee` 87 -> 2946, `block_roots` 69 -> 352.

    EIP-7732 removes `execution_payload` from `BeaconBlockBody`, so the body commits only to an
    execution block hash, at gindex 2856. A Gloas execution proof carries the canonical RLP of
    the execution header, authenticated by `keccak256(bytes) == committed hash`, and the
    `receipts_root` is read out of those authenticated bytes.

    Breaking changes in `snowbridge-beacon-primitives`:

    - `ForkVersions` gains a `gloas` field. Every runtime, mock and benchmark configuration must
      set it.
    - `VersionedExecutionPayloadHeader` gains a `Gloas(BoundedVec<u8, ConstU32<1024>>)` variant.
      It is appended, so existing SCALE encodings continue to decode.
    - `hash_tree_root()`, `receipts_root()`, `block_hash()` and `block_number()` are removed
      from it. `commitment()` replaces them, returning an opaque `ExecutionCommitment`; the
      receipts root is reachable only through the consuming `receipts_root_once_proven()`, so it
      cannot be read off a proof that was never verified.
    - `ForkVersions::is_ordered()` is new: a `const fn` asserting fork epochs are non-decreasing.
      Each schedule asserts it at compile time, so a misordered schedule fails to build.

    In `snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client`, `execution_header_gindex()` becomes
    `execution_commitment_gindex(is_gloas)` and `verify_execution_proof` returns the
    authenticated `receipts_root` instead of `()`. A proof whose variant disagrees with the fork
    era of its beacon header slot is rejected.

    The production fork schedule carries a provisional Sepolia Gloas entry, epoch 351232 and
    version `0x90000076`, neither yet confirmed against `eth-clients/sepolia`.

    Benchmarks run on real Gloas fixtures, which are the worst case. The difference against
    Electra sat below the noise floor, so weights are unchanged; regenerate them on reference
    hardware as usual. Relayer-side changes are separate.
crates:
- name: snowbridge-beacon-primitives
  bump: major
- name: snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client
  bump: major
- name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue
  bump: none
- name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue-v2
  bump: none
- name: bridge-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
